From 1340fbb4e383de75d1d60f4f81b497fd03e7cc33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:03:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] Weight sampled days by weekday, and speak to both
 AeroDataBox plans

A month is never a whole number of weeks. July 2026 has five Wednesdays and
four Sundays, so a seven-day sample that counts both once reads the market
through whichever weekdays it caught -- and since carrier mix moves with the
weekly schedule, that biases every carrier's share. It is the same confound
that made the pilot's single Tuesday read 1.30x. Weighting each sampled day by
its weekday's frequency in the month makes the weights sum to the month's
length exactly, so a sampled week scales to the month rather than resembling
it. A full month weights every day at one, which is the identity.

That matters for what a plan has to cost: a validated weekly sample is 1,624
units against 7,192 for a full month. The direct Starter plan is USD 19 for
40,000 units, half the per-unit cost of RapidAPI's Ultra and ample for one full
validation month plus six sampled weeks. The adapter now resolves host and auth
for either, so choosing a plan does not mean touching code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYLfAv93wjCxnGdihXYpAm
